The most common surprise is the missing @code{date+}. Adding days is
exact and cheap, but it is expressed in day-number space:

@lisp
(tempo:date-from-rata-die
 (+ (tempo:rata-die (tempo:date 2026 12 31)) 1))
@result{} #<DATE 2027-01-01>
@end lisp

@xref{Adding days and spans} for the general recipe. Month arithmetic
is deliberately absent: a month has no fixed number of days, so it
needs a policy for month-end overflow (@pxref{Limits and roadmap}).

