@end deffn

@node Duration Arithmetic
@section Arithmetic

@deffn {Function} duration+ &rest durations
Return the sum of the durations. The months and seconds slots are
summed independently.
@end deffn

@deffn {Function} duration- duration &rest durations
Return @var{duration} minus the remaining durations. With no remaining
arguments, return its negation.
@end deffn

@deffn {Function} duration* a b
@deffnx {Function} duration/ duration divisor
Scale a duration by a real number. @code{duration/} also accepts a
duration as the divisor and then returns the exact ratio of the two
durations. Scaling a months slot must produce a whole number of
months; a zero divisor signals @code{division-by-zero}.
@end deffn

@deffn {Function} duration-divide duration divisor
Return @code{(values quotient remainder-duration)}; the division
truncates toward zero.
@end deffn

@deffn {Function} duration-floor duration &optional resolution
@deffnx {Function} duration-ceiling duration &optional resolution
@deffnx {Function} duration-round duration &optional resolution
Snap @var{duration} to a multiple of @var{resolution}, which defaults
to one second. A duration with calendar months signals
@code{inexact-duration-error}.
@end deffn

@deffn {Function} duration-abs duration
Return the absolute value of @var{duration}. Signals
@code{inexact-duration-error} for a mixed-sign duration.
@end deffn

