@node Date
@chapter Date
@cindex date
@cindex calendar
@cindex weekdays

@deftp {Data Type} date
A proleptic Gregorian calendar date. Constructors validate their
fields: non-integers signal @code{type-error}, while impossible
calendar triples such as February 30 signal @code{invalid-date-error}
with a human-readable reason. Any integer year is accepted, including
0 and negative years.
@end deftp

@lisp
(tempo:date 2026 10 30)
@result{} #<DATE 2026-10-30>
(tempo:next-weekday (tempo:date 2026 10 30) :friday)
@result{} #<DATE 2026-11-06>
@end lisp

@deftp {Data Type} weekday
A weekday keyword from @code{:monday} through @code{:sunday}, or an
abbreviation such as @code{:mon}, @code{:tue}, @code{:wed},
@code{:thu}, @code{:fri}, @code{:sat}, or @code{:sun}.
@end deftp

@deftp {Data Type} weekday-designator
Anything accepted where a weekday is expected: a @code{weekday}
keyword or an integer from 1 (Monday) through 7 (Sunday).
@end deftp

