@deffn {Function} datetime year month day &optional hour minute second
Return a @code{datetime}. Errors from the component constructors
propagate: @code{invalid-date-error} and @code{invalid-time-error} for
impossible values, @code{type-error} for non-numeric ones.
@end deffn

@deffn {Function} make-datetime &key year month day hour minute second
Keyword constructor; @var{year} is required. @var{second} must be a
rational.
@end deffn

@deffn {Function} datetime-from-parts date wall-time
Compose a datetime from an existing date and wall time. The components
are shared, so this performs a single allocation.
@end deffn

@deffn {Function} datetime-p object
Return true when @var{object} is a datetime.
@end deffn

@deffn {Function} datetime-date datetime
@deffnx {Function} datetime-wall-time datetime
Return the stored date or wall time component. Both are shared and
non-allocating.
@end deffn

@deffn {Function} datetime-year datetime
@deffnx {Function} datetime-month datetime
@deffnx {Function} datetime-day datetime
@deffnx {Function} datetime-hour datetime
@deffnx {Function} datetime-minute datetime
@deffnx {Function} datetime-second datetime
Delegating field accessors.
@end deffn

@deffn {Function} valid-datetime-p year month day hour minute second
Return true when the six fields name a real date and time. Total
predicate.
@end deffn

@deffn {Function} destructure-datetime datetime
Return @code{(values year month day hour minute second)}.
@end deffn

@node Datetime Comparisons
@section Comparisons

@deffn {Function} datetime= datetime &rest datetimes
@deffnx {Function} datetime/= datetime &rest datetimes
@deffnx {Function} datetime< datetime &rest datetimes
@deffnx {Function} datetime<= datetime &rest datetimes
@deffnx {Function} datetime> datetime &rest datetimes
@deffnx {Function} datetime>= datetime &rest datetimes
Variadic comparisons, requiring at least one argument. They compare
lexicographically by date fields, then by wall clock fields. The
values are naive; comparing datetimes from different zones is not
meaningful.
@end deffn

@node Datetime Arithmetic
@section Difference and arithmetic

@deffn {Function} datetime+ datetime duration
Return @var{datetime} advanced by @var{duration}'s exact seconds. A
duration with a non-zero months component has no fixed second count and
signals @code{inexact-duration-error}.
@end deffn

@deffn {Function} datetime- datetime duration
Return @var{datetime} adjusted backward by @var{duration}'s exact
seconds.
@end deffn

@deffn {Function} datetime-difference a b
Return the exact duration from @var{b} to @var{a}: the value that,
added to @var{b}, yields @var{a}. Its months component is always zero.
@end deffn

@node Datetime Adjusters
@section Adjusters

@deffn {Function} replace-datetime datetime &key year month day hour minute second
Return a copy of @var{datetime} with any of its six fields replaced.
The @code{clamp-to-end-of-month} restart is available when the day
would overflow the target month
(@pxref{Month-end overflow}).
@end deffn

@deffn {Function} start-of-day datetime
Return midnight of @var{datetime}'s date.
@end deffn

@node Datetime Formatting
@section Formatting

@deffn {Function} write-datetime-to-iso datetime stream
Write @var{datetime} to @var{stream} as an ISO 8601 date and time.
Fractional seconds are printed through a double float, so
non-terminating rationals are approximate.
@end deffn

@deffn {Function} format-datetime-iso datetime
Return @var{datetime} formatted as an ISO 8601 date and time string.
Fractional seconds are printed through a double float, so
non-terminating rationals are approximate.
@end deffn

@deffn {Function} format-datetime stream datetime &optional colon-p at-sign-p
The @code{cl:format} directive function
@code{~/tempo:format-datetime/}.
@end deffn

@node Conditions
@chapter Conditions
@cindex conditions
@cindex restarts

@deffn {Condition} tempo-error
The root of every domain error signalled by @code{tempo}. Establish a single
handler for @code{tempo-error} to catch all of them; see
@ref{Errors and restarts} for the separate @code{type-error} tier.
@end deffn

@deffn {Condition} invalid-date-error
Signalled when year, month, and day do not name a real calendar date.
@end deffn

@deffn {Function} invalid-date-year condition
@deffnx {Function} invalid-date-month condition
@deffnx {Function} invalid-date-day condition
@deffnx {Function} invalid-date-reason condition
Readers for the offending fields and the human-readable reason.
@end deffn

@deffn {Condition} invalid-time-error
Signalled when the hour, minute, or second fields do not name a real
time of day.
@end deffn

@deffn {Function} invalid-time-hour condition
@deffnx {Function} invalid-time-minute condition
@deffnx {Function} invalid-time-second condition
@deffnx {Function} invalid-time-reason condition
Readers for the offending fields and the human-readable reason.
@end deffn

@deffn {Condition} inexact-duration-error
Signalled when an operation needs a fixed number of seconds but the
duration has a calendar months component, or when months and seconds
cannot be compared without a reference date.
@end deffn

@deffn {Function} inexact-duration condition
@deffnx {Function} inexact-duration-reason condition
Readers for the offending duration and the human-readable reason.
@end deffn

@defvr {Restart} clamp-to-end-of-month
Use the last day of the target month. Offered by @code{replace-date}
and @code{replace-datetime} when the day overflows. The @code{date}
constructor does not offer this restart.
@end defvr

@xref{Errors and restarts} for the policy and examples.

@node Formatting
@chapter Formatting
@cindex formatting
@cindex format directives

The per-type @code{write-TYPE-to-iso} and @code{format-TYPE-iso}
functions are documented with each type above. In addition, every
value integrates with @code{cl:format}:

@lisp
(format nil "took ~/tempo:format-duration/" (tempo:hours 2.5))
@result{} "took PT2H30M"
(format nil "at ~/tempo:format-datetime/" (tempo:datetime 2026 10 30 9 30))
@result{} "at 2026-10-30T09:30:00"
@end lisp

@xref{Formatting types} for the printed forms and the ISO
formatting caveats.

